description:
Site: crate-jmap-chat-server/src/chat.rs:156-159.

Code:
    let kind: ChatKind = match serde_json::from_value(Value::String(kind_str.clone())) {
        Ok(k) => k,
        Err(_) => ChatKind::Other(kind_str),
    };

The intent of ChatKind::Other (a #[serde(other)] catch-all variant in jmap-chat-types) is forward-compat at the deserialize boundary: when reading wire data from a future server that knows a new ChatKind variant, the receiver doesn't crash. It is NOT intended as 'accept any client-supplied junk on create'.

This handler accepts:
    Chat/set create {"create": {"x": {"kind": "vampire"}}}
…and stores it. Subsequent Chat/get returns a Chat with kind: 'vampire'. The kind-specific validation (line 166-245) skips required-field checks for unknown kinds (the default arm at line 244 is ), so the Chat lacks contactId/spaceId/anything that would otherwise be required. The result is a junk Chat that breaks every downstream invariant (Message/set chatId pointing at it, Space/changes referencing it).

Spec draft-atwood-jmap-chat-00 §Chat (line 437-449 or thereabouts in the kind discriminator section) enumerates valid kinds. The handler should:
1. Reject unknown kinds with invalidProperties on 'kind'.
2. Reserve ChatKind::Other for deserialize-from-wire fallback only.

Fix:
    let kind = match serde_json::from_value::<ChatKind>(Value::String(kind_str.clone())) {
        Ok(k) if !matches!(k, ChatKind::Other(_)) => k,
        _ => {
            not_created.insert(create_id.clone(), json!({"type": "invalidProperties", "properties": ["kind"]}));
            continue;
        }
    };
